## Deployment

1. Copy files to `{{ base_path }}/{{ role }}/` on the {{ role }} machine
2. Set permissions: `chmod 600 certs/*.key* stores/*.p12`
3. Update `application.yml` with values from `config/application-ssl.yml.snippet`
4. Restart services

## Keystore Password

All keystores and truststores use the same password: configured via `javaSecurityPassword` in setup.properties.
The encrypted form (`ENC(...)`) is used in Spring Boot configuration files.
{% elif role == "mysql" %}
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `certs/server-cert.pem` | MySQL server certificate |
| `certs/server.key` | Server private key (encrypted) |
| `certs/server.key.nopass` | Server private key (unencrypted — MySQL uses this) |
| `certs/ca.pem` | CA certificate |
| `stores/keystore.p12` | PKCS#12 keystore (if needed) |
| `stores/truststore.p12` | PKCS#12 truststore |
| `config/ssl.cnf.snippet` | MySQL SSL configuration |

## Deployment

1. Copy files to `{{ base_path }}/mysql/` on the MySQL machine
2. Set permissions: `chmod 600 certs/*.key*; chown mysql:mysql certs/*`
3. Add SSL config from `config/ssl.cnf.snippet` to `/etc/my.cnf` or `/etc/mysql/mysql.conf.d/ssl.cnf`
4. Restart MySQL: `systemctl restart mysqld`
5. Verify: `mysql -e "SHOW VARIABLES LIKE '%ssl%'"`
{% elif role == "rabbitmq" %}
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `certs/server-cert.pem` | RabbitMQ server certificate |
| `certs/server.key` | Server private key (encrypted) |
| `certs/server.key.nopass` | Server private key (unencrypted — RabbitMQ uses this) |
| `certs/ca.pem` | CA certificate (for verifying client certs) |
| `config/rabbitmq-ssl.conf.snippet` | RabbitMQ TLS configuration |

## Deployment

1. Copy files to `{{ base_path }}/rabbitmq/` on the RabbitMQ machine
2. Set permissions: `chmod 600 certs/*.key*; chown rabbitmq:rabbitmq certs/*`
3. Merge `config/rabbitmq-ssl.conf.snippet` into `/etc/rabbitmq/rabbitmq.conf`
4. Restart RabbitMQ: `systemctl restart rabbitmq-server`
5. Verify: `rabbitmq-diagnostics listeners` (should show port 5671)
{% elif role == "keystone" %}
| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `certs/server-cert.pem` | Keystone server certificate |
| `certs/server.key` | Server private key (encrypted) |
| `certs/server.key.nopass` | Server private key (unencrypted — Apache uses this) |
| `certs/ca.pem` | CA certificate |
| `config/apache-ssl.conf.snippet` | Apache VirtualHost SSL configuration |

## Deployment

1. Copy files to `{{ base_path }}/keystone/` on the Keystone machine
2. Set permissions: `chmod 600 certs/*.key*; chown apache:apache certs/*` (or `www-data`)
3. Merge `config/apache-ssl.conf.snippet` into Keystone's Apache vhost config
4. Enable SSL module: `a2enmod ssl`
5. Restart Apache: `systemctl restart apache2` (or `httpd`)
6. Verify: `curl -v https://{{ hosts.keystone.fqdn }}:5000/v3`
{% endif %}

